---
/**
 * Contact, no forms by design (static, privacy-first site). Points to
 * email and future external spaces.
 */
import PageLayout from '../shared/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import ExternalLink from '../shared/components/ExternalLink.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
import { websiteJsonLd } from '../shared/seo/jsonld';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Contact"
  description="How to reach Satvik.fyi, email for corrections, sources and suggestions. No forms, no tracking."
  path="/contact/"
  eyebrow="Contact"
  lede="Found a mistranslation? A missing source? A practice that deserves more care? These pages improve through exactly that kind of mail."
  jsonLd={[websiteJsonLd(SITE)]}
>
  <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-sand bg-parchment/60 p-6">
      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-earth">Email</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-clay">
        The simplest way to reach the maintainers, corrections, source suggestions and kind
        feedback all welcome.
      </p>
      <a
        href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}
        class="mt-4 inline-block text-sm font-semibold text-saffron-deep underline decoration-saffron/60 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-saffron-deep"
      >
        {SITE.contactEmail}
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-sand bg-parchment/60 p-6">
      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-earth">Corrections policy</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-clay">
        When we get a citation or translation wrong, we fix the page and note the change. When a
        tradition is misrepresented, we consult the sources again before writing back.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-dashed border-sand bg-parchment/50 p-6">
    <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-earth">Why no contact form?</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-clay">
      This is a static site: no server, no database, no personal data stored. Forms would require
      both. A mailbox does the same job without either. When the newsletter and community spaces
      launch, they will live with external services (Substack, Discord or similar) on their own
      terms, linked from the <ExternalLink class="text-saffron-deep underline underline-offset-4" href="https://substack.com">footer</ExternalLink>, never embedded here.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
